Annex A: Record, Version, and Metadata Schemas {#annex-a}
==========================================

## Record Schema ## {#annex-record-schema}

The JSON Schema for the [=Record=], Version and Metadata structures is published at <https://recordweb.org/…> with the identifier `$id`. This version of RWP refers to the file with the SHA-256 value `sha256:…`.


### Root Agent ### {#annex-root-agent}

The <dfn>Root Agent</dfn> is the [=AgentRecord=] of the **RecordWeb Trust Association**. It is the initial controller of the Root Schemas ([[#annex-root-schemas]]). It is the owner of the Root Schemas, and the DID documents of the Root Schemas name it as controller.

<table class="data">
<thead><tr><th>Name<th>DID<th>versionHash of the Record<th>versionHash of the first DID document</thead>
<tr><td>RecordWeb Trust Association<td><code>did:rwp:d2d14675-50c9-463d-b564-1ea50644c836:agent-recordweb-trust-association</code><td><code>sha256:…</code><td><code>sha256:…</code>
</table>

The `versionHash` of the Record identifies the version of the [=AgentRecord=] that applies to this version of RWP. The `versionHash` of the first DID document identifies the first version of its DID document, which publishes the initial verification methods. A verifier MAY use this value as the starting point of the verification of the DID document history ([[#section-didoc-verification]]).

A later version of the [=AgentRecord=] or of its DID document is not part of this version of RWP. A change of verification methods creates a new DID document version ([[#section-didoc-history]]) and does not require a new version of RWP.

Trust assumptions of RWP are defined in [[#section-federation-trust-anchor]].


## Root Schemas ## {#annex-root-schemas}

A [=Root Schema=] is a [=SchemaRecord=] listed in the following table. A [=SchemaRecord=] is a Root Schema only if its DID is listed here. The column `versionHash` identifies the version of the Root Schema that applies to this version of RWP.

A later version of the same [=SchemaRecord=], reachable from this version through `previousSchemaVersion`, is not part of this version of RWP. Whether and when an implementation adopts a later version is the decision of the implementation. RWP makes no statement about conformance to a later version before a later version of RWP lists it. A [=Record=] is validated against the version of its [=SchemaRecord=] identified by `metadata.core.schemaVersion`.

<table class="data">
<thead><tr><th>Record type<th>DID<th>versionHash</thead>
<tr><td>SchemaRecord<td><code>did:rwp:d2d14675-50c9-463d-b564-1ea50644c836:schema-root-schemarecord</code><td><code>sha256:…</code>
<tr><td>AgentRecord<td><code>did:rwp:d2d14675-50c9-463d-b564-1ea50644c836:schema-root-agentrecord</code><td><code>sha256:…</code>
<tr><td>CaseRecord<td><code>did:rwp:d2d14675-50c9-463d-b564-1ea50644c836:schema-root-caserecord</code><td><code>sha256:…</code>
<tr><td>AssertionRecord<td><code>did:rwp:d2d14675-50c9-463d-b564-1ea50644c836:schema-root-assertionrecord</code><td><code>sha256:…</code>
<tr><td>DeletionRecord<td><code>did:rwp:d2d14675-50c9-463d-b564-1ea50644c836:schema-root-deletionrecord</code><td><code>sha256:…</code>
</table>

Where the text of this specification and a Root Schema identified in this annex differ, the Root Schema prevails.

